    caution: 'Watch out: fewer openings than government posts, and most roles want 2-4 years of experience or a strong MLIS project portfolio first.',
  },
  {
    badge: '02',
    title: 'Digital archiving and digital-repository specialist',
    body: 'Universities, cultural and heritage institutions, government digitisation missions, and corporates need people who can build and maintain digital repositories, metadata standards, and long-term preservation systems, not just shelve physical books.',
    positive: 'Best for: LIS graduates who also build real technical skill in metadata standards, repository software, and basic database work.',
    caution: 'Watch out: still a smaller job market than traditional librarian posts, so most people build this alongside a salaried library role first.',
  },
  {
    badge: '03',
    title: 'University and academic librarian (post-UGC-NET)',
    body: 'Owns a college or university library\'s full collection, research support, and reader services, with a real promotion ladder up to university librarian at senior institutions.',
    positive: 'Best for: people who want a structured, senior academic-sector ceiling and do not mind a multi-stage qualifying process.',
    caution: 'Watch out: the entry gate is genuinely competitive, covered in full in the UGC-NET section below.',
  },
  {
    badge: '04',
    title: 'Government and public library service',
    body: 'State library departments, central government libraries such as the National Library and Delhi Public Library, and public-sector research institutions recruit librarians and library assistants on fixed government pay scales.',
